<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_StrandedDeformation.xml            UtinniPatches - COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1

  Resolves ledger slug
  `the_miasma:the-stranded-transitional-orphan-forms-2-3-species`
  (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/the_miasma.md §4: "the surge's orphans:
  endemics cut off in pools when the salt line moves, forced ashore between
  waters - gills going leathery, fins splaying into feet that don't quite
  work. Creatures that look transitional: evolution auditioning, generation
  by generation, in the pools behind the player's base").

  Per the owner's ruling recorded in miasma_fauna_roster_2026-09-23.md §5
  ("decision taken by question card"): the stranded are the sea nursery's
  FAILURES, not their own species - "nothing below is a new animal." This
  file is that condition: a permanent Hediff applied to a minority of the
  ordinary nursery juveniles a stranding pool already spawns (the roster's
  own §5 table, "the deformation" row), never a new creature or PawnKindDef.

  Read this together with the C# half of the same slug
  (RM_StrandingPoolsExtension.strandedDeformationHediff/
  strandedDeformationChance, RM_MapComponent_StrandingPools.
  SpawnStrandedInto, RM_JobGiver_ReturnToWater.TryGiveJob - all three edited
  this pass, src/RimMandrake/EnvironmentalHazards/Source/): a pawn carrying
  this hediff is deliberately EXCLUDED from the JobGiver's existing
  rescue-by-pathing behaviour ("it cannot return to water, and it does not
  thrive" - roster §5), which is why the mechanical effects below lean on
  Moving/Metabolism rather than anything cosmetic.

  🔴 THE LOOK (an altered sprite - "gills going leathery, fins splaying into
  feet") is explicitly flagged UNMEASURABLE ON THE MAC by the roster itself
  (§7: "how much a hediff can change an animal's rendered appearance") and
  is NOT attempted here - same "never block on an unmeasured visual" posture
  this repo's own flight law and DarkCrust/FleetFlier precedent already use
  for missing frames/art. The condition is real and mechanical; the sprite
  stays the juvenile's own, pending a Desktop check.

  hediffClass plain Hediff (not HediffWithComps): no comp is needed - the
  severity never changes on its own (isBad permanent condition, not a
  disease with a progression curve), and the JobGiver-suppression half of
  this mechanism lives in C#, not in a HediffComp.

  minSeverity/initialSeverity 1 with a single stage and no upper bound: this
  is a fixed condition from the moment of stranding, not something that
  ramps - matching the roster's own framing ("a condition... not a new
  species," applied once at spawn, never re-rolled).

  Capacity effects, INVENTED-BUILD (no figures named by the roster beyond
  the qualitative "does not thrive" and "half-working gait"): Moving -35%
  (splayed, not-quite-working limbs), Metabolism -15% (poorly adapted to
  either environment, per "auditioning" framing), Breathing -10% (leathery,
  imperfect gills). Deliberately NOT lethal on its own (no lethalSeverity) -
  the roster's own "pay-off... occasionally survives into something that
  works" implies the condition itself must not be a death sentence; being
  stuck in a drying, undefended pool is what does the killing, same as an
  ordinary (non-deformed) stranded pawn already risks today.
-->
<Defs>

  <HediffDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_StrandedDeformation</defName>
    <label>stranded deformation</label>
    <labelNoun>a stranded deformation</labelNoun>
    <description>Gills gone leathery, fins splaying toward something that almost works as a foot. Left ashore too long by a retreating salt line, this one is not going back - and it is not quite built for staying, either.</description>
    <hediffClass>Hediff</hediffClass>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.55,0.62,0.35)</defaultLabelColor>
    <isBad>true</isBad>
    <minSeverity>1</minSeverity>
    <initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <makesSickThought>false</makesSickThought>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>transitional</label>
        <painOffset>0.03</painOffset>
        <statOffsets>
          <MoveSpeed>-0.6</MoveSpeed>
        </statOffsets>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>-0.35</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Metabolism</capacity>
            <offset>-0.15</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Breathing</capacity>
            <offset>-0.10</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
